Topi Linkala wrote:

> I second this. But when I create a stash I burn
> Elbereth, drop a cursed item and put the container
> on top. I've never had a pet to pick up the
> container on such square. Have I've been lucky?

Probably, but not fantastically so, the odds are
pretty much in your favor anyway. Your pet ignores
Elbereth even with something on top of it, of
course, as do peaceful monsters. IIRC from very long
ago source diving, the "steps reluctantly" only
happens after the pet attempts unsuccessfully
several times to take a step somewhere not
obstructed or containing a cursed object [so it
happens a lot more in a passageway than in the
middle of a room, more at the edge of a room than in
the middle of the room].

Second, if you put enough crud in the container, the
pet won't be able to lift it anyway (but watch out
for warhorses, they lift really heavy chests).

Otherwise, I think you've still got the situation
where your pet will cart off your stash even on top
of a cursed item, if you're rather profoundly
unlucky, but not with a cursed item on top, ever.

You have to weigh that risk against the convenience
of having the tool glyph or the chest icon visible
when you return to the level after long absences.

FWIW

